---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="PMO Lead and automation developer at a professional services firm, working where operations, reporting, and technology meet."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>
        I build the infrastructure that makes a professional services firm run.
      </h1>

      <div class="about__intro">
        <figure class="about__portrait">
          <img
            src="/images/marisol.jpg"
            alt="Marisol Delbrey"
            width="1024"
            height="1280"
          />
        </figure>

        <div class="prose stack">
          <p>
            I'm a PMO Lead at a full-service professional services firm, where I
            report directly to the COO and work closely with the managing partner
            and partners across the firm. I automate workflows, build reporting
            systems, and lead projects from intake to delivery. Most days I'm
            looking at data, writing SQL, or debugging a flow that was working
            fine yesterday.
          </p>

          <p>
            My path into this work ran through <a
              href="https://breakthroughtech.org">Breakthrough Tech AI</a
            >, a competitive fellowship at UCLA, a case competition with
            Accenture, and a machine learning certification from Cornell.
            Accenture is where I figured out what I actually wanted: not
            technology for its own sake, and not operations without the technical
            depth to change it. I graduated from Chapman University with a degree
            in Philosophy and a Computer Science minor, which is either a strange
            combination or exactly the right one for this kind of work.
          </p>

          <p>
            I connect systems that weren't built to talk to each other. Right now
            that means a Karbon API feeding a collections dashboard, a Snowflake
            data layer replacing one-off exports, and a client intake flow that
            routes from CRM into practice management automatically when an
            opportunity closes. I also automate monthly balanced scorecards for
            the full firm and build CRM reporting flows that used to run on
            manual exports. Most of these projects started because someone
            noticed a gap and asked if it was fixable. The answer is usually yes,
            it just takes longer than expected.
          </p>

          <p>
            I was recently invited to speak as a panelist at our firm's State of
            the Firm event. I'll be the youngest person on that stage. That's not
            something I expected this early, and it's the kind of moment that
            tells you you're doing something right.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section about-details">
    <div class="wrap grid grid--2">
      <div>
        <h2 class="eyebrow">Focus areas</h2>
        <ul class="plain-list">
          <li>Project Management Office</li>
          <li>Workflow Automation</li>
          <li>AI Implementation</li>
          <li>Data Reporting and Operations</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="eyebrow">Background</h2>
        <ul class="plain-list">
          <li>PMO Lead, Professional Services Firm, 2025 to present</li>
          <li>Strategy and Technology Intern, Accenture</li>
          <li>
            PMP Candidate (exam target September 2026); Machine Learning
            Certification, Cornell University
          </li>
          <li>B.A. Philosophy, Computer Science Minor, Chapman University</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section about-cta">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="lead">
        I'm always open to conversations about operations, automation, and AI in
        professional services.
      </p>
      <a class="button button--accent" href="/contact/">Get in touch</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Portrait sits under the heading on phones and beside the copy on desktop.
     It is first in the DOM so it stays next to the heading when stacked. */
  .about__intro {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    align-items: start;
  }

  @media (min-width: 52rem) {
    .about__intro {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 0.6fr;
    }

    .about__portrait {
      grid-column: 2;
      grid-row: 1;
    }
  }

  .about__portrait {
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Landscape source cropped to portrait; matches the hero framing. */
  .about__portrait img {
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: 47% 35%;
    border-radius: 2px;
  }

  .about-details,
  .about-cta {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .plain-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .plain-list li {
    padding: 0.6rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .about-cta .lead {
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
  }
</style>
